1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,600
Landing on the moon isn't just about where.

2
00:00:02,930 --> 00:00:04,070
It's about when.

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,570
At the lunar south pole, sunlight means power.

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:10,390
A clear view of Earth means communication.

5
00:00:10,870 --> 00:00:12,350
Meet Polaris Window.

6
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:15,140
Built using NASA terrain and orbital data,

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:19,020
it lets you explore real lunar landscapes, compare locations,

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,380
and discover promising landing windows.

9
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:25,140
From complex scientific data to clearer mission decisions.

10
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:26,520
Polaris Window.

11
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,440
Find your window to the moon.
